# .tfvalidate-ignore — tracked exceptions for validate_terraform.py
#
# One check ID per line. Optionally scope to a path by adding a substring
# after the ID — the ignore only applies to modules whose path contains it.
# Unscoped lines ignore that check everywhere in the repo.
#
# Keep this file reviewed like any other config: an ignore that's no longer
# justified should be deleted, not left to rot.
#
# Check ID scheme:
#   T-series  Terraform/HashiCorp code conventions
#   A-series  AWS/infrastructure best practices
#   P-series  PDS/PDC-specific requirements
#   S-series  Should-Have recommendations
#
# Examples:
#
# P6                          ignore the state-bucket-naming check everywhere
#                              (e.g. repo predates the pds-<venue>-infra convention
#                              and a rename is tracked separately in JIRA-1234)
#
# P15  opensearch_managed      ignore the default_tags check only for modules
#                              whose path contains "opensearch_managed"
#
# P20  legacy_bucket           ignore the org-module check for a single legacy module
#                              while migration to pds-tf-modules is in progress
